::STAT_U02_L03_Q01::
Question ID: STAT_U02_L03_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.DVD.4
Question:
Two data sets have the same median. Set A has range 6, and Set B has range 24. Which is more consistent?
{
=A. Set A#Correct. The smaller range means less variability.
~B. Set B#Set B has greater spread.
~C. Both are equally consistent#The ranges are not equal.
~D. Cannot compare because medians match#Variability can still be compared.
}

::STAT_U02_L03_Q02::
Question ID: STAT_U02_L03_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.DVD.4
Question:
Which measure of center is usually more resistant to an outlier?
{
~A. Mean#Mean can be pulled by outliers.
=B. Median#Correct. The median is based on position and is less affected by extreme values.
~C. Range#Range measures spread and is very affected by outliers.
~D. Maximum#Maximum may be the outlier.
}

::STAT_U02_L03_Q03::
Question ID: STAT_U02_L03_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.DVD.4
Question:
What should you compare in addition to center when comparing data sets?
{
~A. File name#The file name is not a statistical summary.
~B. Answer letters#Answer letters are assessment formatting.
=C. Variability#Correct. Spread helps describe consistency and differences beyond center.
~D. Font size#Font size is not data evidence.
}

::STAT_U02_L03_Q04::
Question ID: STAT_U02_L03_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.DVD.4
Question:
Which value is a possible outlier in 8, 9, 10, 11, 35?
{
~A. 8#8 is near the rest of the low values.
~B. 10#10 is in the center of the cluster.
~C. 11#11 is near the cluster.
=D. 35#Correct. 35 is far from the cluster of values from 8 to 11.
}

::STAT_U02_L03_Q05::
Question ID: STAT_U02_L03_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.DVD.4
Question:
Why should outliers not be automatically deleted?
{
=A. They may represent meaningful real data#Correct. Outliers should be investigated in context before deciding how to handle them.
~B. They never affect summaries#Outliers can affect mean and range.
~C. They are always errors#Some outliers are valid observations.
~D. They only affect categorical data#Outliers are unusual numerical values.
}

